    {
      "stem": "What is Data Leakage in Machine Learning, and why can it make a model appear more accurate during testing than it will be in real-world use?",
      "tag": "Beginner · Core definition",
      "answer": "b",
      "options": [
        "Data leakage occurs when strongly predictive features are included during training, even when those features are available before every real prediction. This makes evaluation scores unreliable.",
        "Data Leakage occurs when a model uses information that should not be available during training or prediction. This can produce artificially high evaluation scores and poor performance on new data.",
        "Data leakage occurs when a model is evaluated on unfamiliar test records after training, because using any held-out data to measure performance introduces forbidden information.",
        "Data leakage occurs when duplicate examples cross dataset splits, but using future events to build training features remains acceptable if the records themselves are different."
      ],
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> Data leakage happens when a model learns from information it would not have when making a real prediction. Testing then becomes unfairly easy, making the score look better than the model's true ability. Imagine a bank predicting whether a loan will be repaid. If its training data includes a collection notice created after someone misses payments, the model has effectively seen the future. That notice will not exist when a new loan application arrives, so the impressive test score may collapse in practice.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"g2-figure\"><span class=\"g2-kicker\">VISUAL 01 · DATA LEAKAGE</span><h3>A score mirage from future information</h3><div class=\"g2-canvas\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 940 370\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two sample results: 97 percent with leakage and 68 percent on a realistic future holdout; percentages illustrate the phenomenon rather than actual performance measurements\"><rect x=\"1\" y=\"1\" width=\"938\" height=\"368\" rx=\"17\" fill=\"#fcfeff\" stroke=\"#d6e7eb\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"44\" fill=\"#1f4054\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"900\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">A SCORE THAT LOOKS TOO GOOD</text><rect x=\"43\" y=\"73\" width=\"410\" height=\"237\" rx=\"19\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#d5e4e9\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"75\" y=\"113\" fill=\"#cc6963\" font-size=\"23\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Leaky testing</text><rect x=\"93\" y=\"148\" width=\"267\" height=\"31\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"#ffebe9\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"93\" y=\"148\" width=\"259\" height=\"31\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"#cc6963\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"379\" y=\"174\" fill=\"#cc6963\" font-size=\"27\" font-weight=\"900\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">97%</text><text x=\"72\" y=\"223\" fill=\"#567080\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Future outcome accidentally</text><text x=\"72\" y=\"250\" fill=\"#567080\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">revealed during training</text><rect x=\"492\" y=\"73\" width=\"408\" height=\"237\" rx=\"19\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#d5e4e9\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"523\" y=\"113\" fill=\"#138477\" font-size=\"23\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Real future holdout</text><rect x=\"546\" y=\"148\" width=\"267\" height=\"31\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"#e4f5ed\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"546\" y=\"148\" width=\"181\" height=\"31\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"#138477\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"835\" y=\"174\" fill=\"#138477\" font-size=\"27\" font-weight=\"900\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">68%</text><text x=\"519\" y=\"223\" fill=\"#567080\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Only prediction-time facts</text><text x=\"519\" y=\"250\" fill=\"#567080\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Illustrative values only</text><rect x=\"305\" y=\"320\" width=\"335\" height=\"34\" rx=\"17\" fill=\"#fff2db\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"472.5\" y=\"343\" fill=\"#93692a\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"800\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Leakage can inflate an evaluation</text></svg></div><p class=\"g2-note\">High scores may be misleading when target outcomes or future events appear among the training inputs.</p></section>"
    },
    {
      "stem": "What are Target Leakage and Train-Test Contamination, and how do these two types of Data Leakage differ?",
      "tag": "Beginner · Leakage types",
      "answer": "d",
      "options": [
        "Target Leakage occurs when a test label guides preprocessing, while Train-Test Contamination occurs when a feature reveals an outcome that will not exist at prediction time.",
        "Target Leakage occurs when a feature is highly predictive, even if it is available before the decision. Train-Test Contamination requires directly copying test labels into training.",
        "Target Leakage occurs when future target details appear in features, while Train-Test Contamination happens only when identical rows appear in both sets, not when test statistics influence preprocessing.",
        "Target Leakage occurs when a feature reveals target information unavailable at prediction time. Train-Test Contamination occurs when information from test data influences model training or preprocessing."
      ],
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> Target leakage means an input reveals the outcome using information unavailable when a prediction must be made. Train-test contamination is different: information from the test set reaches training or preprocessing, so the test is no longer independent. Imagine predicting which hospital patients will be readmitted. Using a future follow-up code is target leakage. Calculating a preprocessing statistic using both training patients and test patients is contamination. One leaks future outcome information; the other leaks evaluation-set information.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"g2-figure\"><span class=\"g2-kicker\">VISUAL 02 · DATA LEAKAGE</span><h3>Two different ways information crosses a boundary</h3><div class=\"g2-canvas\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 940 370\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Target leakage feeds a later collection notice into a loan model, while test contamination feeds held-out statistics into a scaler fit\"><rect x=\"1\" y=\"1\" width=\"938\" height=\"368\" rx=\"17\" fill=\"#fcfeff\" stroke=\"#d6e7eb\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"43\" y=\"43\" fill=\"#cc6963\" font-size=\"21\" font-weight=\"900\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">TARGET LEAKAGE</text><text x=\"510\" y=\"43\" fill=\"#4c83bb\" font-size=\"21\" font-weight=\"900\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">TRAIN–TEST CONTAMINATION</text><rect x=\"39\" y=\"68\" width=\"401\" height=\"254\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"#ffebe9\" stroke=\"#ecc3bf\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"67\" y=\"112\" width=\"138\" height=\"89\" rx=\"13\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#e5bdb9\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"136\" y=\"148\" fill=\"#1f4054\" font-size=\"22\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Loan</text><text x=\"136\" y=\"177\" fill=\"#567080\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"650\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">application</text><rect x=\"260\" y=\"112\" width=\"148\" height=\"89\" rx=\"13\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#e5bdb9\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"334\" y=\"148\" fill=\"#cc6963\" font-size=\"21\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Collection</text><text x=\"334\" y=\"177\" fill=\"#567080\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"650\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">notice later</text><path d=\"M328 215Q239 286 148 218\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#cc6963\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 7\"/><text x=\"238\" y=\"295\" fill=\"#cc6963\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Future outcome enters features</text><rect x=\"484\" y=\"68\" width=\"420\" height=\"254\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"#eaf5fc\" stroke=\"#bed8e7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"518\" y=\"112\" width=\"147\" height=\"91\" rx=\"13\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#b9d8e3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"592\" y=\"149\" fill=\"#138477\" font-size=\"22\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">TRAIN</text><text x=\"592\" y=\"178\" fill=\"#567080\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"650\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">fit scaler</text><rect x=\"738\" y=\"112\" width=\"139\" height=\"91\" rx=\"13\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#b9d8e3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"806\" y=\"149\" fill=\"#4c83bb\" font-size=\"22\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">TEST</text><text x=\"806\" y=\"178\" fill=\"#567080\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"650\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">held out</text><path d=\"M789 218Q687 291 592 218\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#cc6963\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 7\"/><text x=\"695\" y=\"295\" fill=\"#cc6963\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Test statistics influence fit</text></svg></div><p class=\"g2-note\">Target leakage uses unavailable outcome clues. Train–test contamination lets held-out information influence training.</p></section>"
    },
    {
      "stem": "Why must preprocessing methods such as scaling, missing-value imputation, and feature selection be fitted only on training data rather than the entire dataset?",
      "tag": "Beginner · Preprocessing boundary",
      "answer": "a",
      "options": [
        "Fitting preprocessing methods on the entire dataset allows test information to influence the model. Fitting them only on training data keeps test data independent and produces more reliable evaluation results.",
        "Preprocessing should use the full dataset before splitting when it does not read target labels, because estimating scaling or imputation statistics from test inputs cannot affect evaluation.",
        "Preprocessing should be fitted separately on training and test data so each group receives its own scaling, missing-value replacements, and selected features during the final evaluation.",
        "Preprocessing can be fitted on all available rows after the train-test split as long as the estimator is trained only on training labels and the test labels remain hidden."
      ],
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> Preprocessing can learn information from data, even when it is not learning model weights. A scaler learns averages, an imputer learns replacement values, and feature selection learns which inputs look useful. If these decisions use the test set, its information has influenced training. Imagine predicting apartment rents: calculate the median floor area from training apartments only, then use that same value for missing entries in test apartments. Split first, fit on training data, and transform the test data without refitting.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"g2-figure\"><span class=\"g2-kicker\">VISUAL 03 · DATA LEAKAGE</span><h3>One set of training statistics</h3><div class=\"g2-canvas\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 940 370\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Median of training ages 20 and 30 is 25; a test age 90 does not contribute to this fitted median\"><rect x=\"1\" y=\"1\" width=\"938\" height=\"368\" rx=\"17\" fill=\"#fcfeff\" stroke=\"#d6e7eb\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"45\" y=\"47\" fill=\"#138477\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"900\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">FIT ONLY ON TRAINING AGES</text><text x=\"611\" y=\"47\" fill=\"#4c83bb\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"900\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">KEEP TEST UNSEEN</text><rect x=\"42\" y=\"70\" width=\"480\" height=\"241\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"#e4f5ed\" stroke=\"#b5dacc\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"72\" y=\"115\" width=\"181\" height=\"76\" rx=\"13\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#b5dacc\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"163\" y=\"150\" fill=\"#138477\" font-size=\"30\" font-weight=\"900\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">20</text><text x=\"163\" y=\"177\" fill=\"#567080\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"650\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Training</text><rect x=\"278\" y=\"115\" width=\"181\" height=\"76\" rx=\"13\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#b5dacc\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"370\" y=\"150\" fill=\"#138477\" font-size=\"30\" font-weight=\"900\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">30</text><text x=\"370\" y=\"177\" fill=\"#567080\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"650\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Training</text><text x=\"276\" y=\"239\" fill=\"#1f4054\" font-size=\"29\" font-weight=\"900\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Median = 25</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"263\" width=\"358\" height=\"34\" rx=\"17\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"279\" y=\"286\" fill=\"#138477\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"800\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Use 25 for a missing test age</text><path d=\"M565 72V311\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#cc6963\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"7 7\"/><rect x=\"606\" y=\"70\" width=\"291\" height=\"241\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"#eaf5fc\" stroke=\"#bed9e5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"749\" y=\"134\" fill=\"#4c83bb\" font-size=\"41\" font-weight=\"900\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">90</text><text x=\"749\" y=\"171\" fill=\"#567080\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Held-out test age</text><text x=\"749\" y=\"226\" fill=\"#cc6963\" font-size=\"22\" font-weight=\"900\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">NOT used to fit</text><text x=\"749\" y=\"260\" fill=\"#567080\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"650\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Transform afterward</text></svg></div><p class=\"g2-note\">Fit statistics using training records. Later, reuse those fitted statistics on held-out records.</p></section>"
    },
    {
      "stem": "How can Data Leakage occur during cross-validation when preprocessing, feature selection, or data augmentation is performed before creating validation folds?",
      "tag": "Medium · Cross-validation folds",
      "answer": "c",
      "options": [
        "Cross-validation prevents leakage once folds are created, so fitting a scaler or feature selector on the entire dataset beforehand is safe if the target labels were not used.",
        "Data augmentation can occur before creating validation folds when the transformed examples retain their original labels, because those new examples count as independent observations.",
        "Leakage occurs when preprocessing or feature selection uses validation data, or when related augmented samples appear in both training and validation folds. These operations must respect training and validation boundaries.",
        "Feature engineering can use every validation fold to identify useful features, provided the final model is fitted only on its training fold and scored on held-out labels."
      ],
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> Cross-validation works only when each validation fold stays unseen during fitting. If you select features or calculate scaling statistics before making folds, every validation fold has already influenced those choices. Data augmentation can also leak nearly identical examples across folds. Imagine creating rotated copies of product photos before cross-validation: the original image might land in training and its rotated twin in validation. The score then measures recognition of a familiar image, not generalization. Make folds first and fit transformations using each fold's training portion.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"g2-figure\"><span class=\"g2-kicker\">VISUAL 04 · DATA LEAKAGE</span><h3>Fold boundaries must survive augmentation</h3><div class=\"g2-canvas\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 940 370\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Four cross-validation folds rotate validation status; original image A and rotated image A stay within the same fold\"><rect x=\"1\" y=\"1\" width=\"938\" height=\"368\" rx=\"17\" fill=\"#fcfeff\" stroke=\"#d6e7eb\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"42\" fill=\"#1f4054\" font-size=\"21\" font-weight=\"900\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">THE VALIDATION FOLD ROTATES</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"113\" fill=\"#567080\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Fold 1</text><rect x=\"141\" y=\"86\" width=\"115\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#d4953c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"198\" y=\"112\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">VALIDATE</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"86\" width=\"115\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#138477\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"327\" y=\"112\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">TRAIN</text><rect x=\"399\" y=\"86\" width=\"115\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#138477\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"456\" y=\"112\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">TRAIN</text><rect x=\"528\" y=\"86\" width=\"115\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#138477\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"585\" y=\"112\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">TRAIN</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"167\" fill=\"#567080\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Fold 2</text><rect x=\"141\" y=\"140\" width=\"115\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#138477\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"198\" y=\"166\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">TRAIN</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"140\" width=\"115\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#d4953c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"327\" y=\"166\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">VALIDATE</text><rect x=\"399\" y=\"140\" width=\"115\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#138477\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"456\" y=\"166\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">TRAIN</text><rect x=\"528\" y=\"140\" width=\"115\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#138477\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"585\" y=\"166\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">TRAIN</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"221\" fill=\"#567080\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Fold 3</text><rect x=\"141\" y=\"194\" width=\"115\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#138477\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"198\" y=\"220\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">TRAIN</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"194\" width=\"115\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#138477\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"327\" y=\"220\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">TRAIN</text><rect x=\"399\" y=\"194\" width=\"115\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#d4953c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"456\" y=\"220\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">VALIDATE</text><rect x=\"528\" y=\"194\" width=\"115\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#138477\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"585\" y=\"220\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">TRAIN</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"275\" fill=\"#567080\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"750\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Fold 4</text><rect x=\"141\" y=\"248\" width=\"115\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#138477\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"198\" y=\"274\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">TRAIN</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"248\" width=\"115\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#138477\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"327\" y=\"274\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">TRAIN</text><rect x=\"399\" y=\"248\" width=\"115\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#138477\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"456\" y=\"274\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">TRAIN</text><rect x=\"528\" y=\"248\" width=\"115\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#d4953c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"585\" y=\"274\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">VALIDATE</text><rect x=\"690\" y=\"66\" width=\"219\" height=\"260\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"#fff2db\" stroke=\"#e8ce9e\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"798\" y=\"102\" fill=\"#926725\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">AUGMENTATION</text><rect x=\"721\" y=\"125\" width=\"159\" height=\"62\" rx=\"13\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"800\" y=\"163\" fill=\"#1f4054\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"800\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Original A</text><rect x=\"721\" y=\"214\" width=\"159\" height=\"62\" rx=\"13\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"800\" y=\"253\" fill=\"#1f4054\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"800\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Rotated A</text><path d=\"M800 189V211\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#d4953c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"800\" y=\"305\" fill=\"#cc6963\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Keep variants together</text></svg></div><p class=\"g2-note\">Augmented relatives are not independent observations; do not distribute them across train and validation.</p></section>"
