    {
      "stem": "How do Scikit-learn Pipelines and proper train-test splitting help prevent Data Leakage during Machine Learning model development?",
      "tag": "Medium · Leakage-safe pipelines",
      "answer": "b",
      "options": [
        "Scikit-learn Pipelines prevent leakage by learning common scaling and feature-selection settings from all available records first, then running the classifier on each separate training split.",
        "Scikit-learn Pipelines fit preprocessing and model steps using only training data within each split. Proper train-test splitting prevents evaluation data from influencing the training process.",
        "Proper splitting makes independent preprocessing unnecessary because separately applying feature selection to the held-out test data preserves the same features without exposing its labels.",
        "A Pipeline automatically protects the final test set even when feature selection and missing-value imputation were already fitted outside the Pipeline using all available data."
      ],
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> A Scikit-learn Pipeline keeps preprocessing and model fitting together, so each cross-validation training fold learns its own imputation values, scaling statistics, and selected features. Its validation fold is transformed using those learned settings, not used to fit them. First reserve a separate test set, then cross-validate the Pipeline on training data. For example, an email-spam classifier might select useful words from each training fold only. That prevents the validation emails from influencing which words were chosen and gives a fairer performance estimate.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"g2-figure\"><span class=\"g2-kicker\">VISUAL 05 · DATA LEAKAGE</span><h3>The Pipeline lives inside cross-validation</h3><div class=\"g2-canvas\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 940 370\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Imputation, scaling, selection, and estimator fit inside each training fold, followed by validation-only scoring\"><rect x=\"1\" y=\"1\" width=\"938\" height=\"368\" rx=\"17\" fill=\"#fcfeff\" stroke=\"#d6e7eb\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"42\" y=\"43\" fill=\"#138477\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"900\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">REFIT ALL STEPS INSIDE EACH TRAINING FOLD</text><rect x=\"37\" y=\"71\" width=\"670\" height=\"233\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"#e4f5ed\" stroke=\"#acd8c9\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"64\" y=\"125\" width=\"137\" height=\"111\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#b6d8d1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"132\" y=\"168\" fill=\"#1f4054\" font-size=\"22\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Impute</text><text x=\"132\" y=\"200\" fill=\"#138477\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">fit / transform</text><path d=\"M203 178L223 178\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#138477\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M212.46900925731552 183.75310646325045L223 178L212.46900925731552 172.24689353674955\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#138477\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><rect x=\"224\" y=\"125\" width=\"137\" height=\"111\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#b6d8d1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"292\" y=\"168\" fill=\"#1f4054\" font-size=\"22\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Scale</text><text x=\"292\" y=\"200\" fill=\"#138477\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">fit / transform</text><path d=\"M363 178L383 178\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#138477\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M372.4690092573155 183.75310646325045L383 178L372.4690092573155 172.24689353674955\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#138477\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><rect x=\"384\" y=\"125\" width=\"137\" height=\"111\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#b6d8d1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"452\" y=\"168\" fill=\"#1f4054\" font-size=\"22\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Select</text><text x=\"452\" y=\"200\" fill=\"#138477\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">fit / transform</text><path d=\"M523 178L543 178\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#138477\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M532.4690092573155 183.75310646325045L543 178L532.4690092573155 172.24689353674955\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#138477\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><rect x=\"544\" y=\"125\" width=\"137\" height=\"111\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#b6d8d1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"612\" y=\"168\" fill=\"#1f4054\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Train model</text><text x=\"612\" y=\"200\" fill=\"#138477\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">fit</text><rect x=\"733\" y=\"71\" width=\"172\" height=\"233\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"#eaf5fc\" stroke=\"#bed9e8\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"819\" y=\"155\" fill=\"#4c83bb\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">VALIDATE</text><text x=\"819\" y=\"191\" fill=\"#567080\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"650\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">transform</text><text x=\"819\" y=\"215\" fill=\"#567080\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"650\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">and score</text><path d=\"M708 178L730 178\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4c83bb\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M719.4690092573155 183.75310646325045L730 178L719.4690092573155 172.24689353674955\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4c83bb\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><rect x=\"165\" y=\"317\" width=\"620\" height=\"34\" rx=\"17\" fill=\"#fff2db\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"475\" y=\"340\" fill=\"#956923\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"800\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">cross_val_score refits each full Pipeline per fold</text></svg></div><p class=\"g2-note\">A Pipeline prevents leakage only when preprocessing and selection happen inside it.</p><section class=\"g2-code\" aria-label=\"Runnable scikit-learn Pipeline example\"><div class=\"g2-code-label\">PYTHON · LEAKAGE-SAFE CROSS-VALIDATION</div><pre><code>from sklearn.datasets import make_classification\nfrom sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\nfrom sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\nfrom sklearn.feature_selection import SelectKBest, f_classif\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import cross_val_score\n\nX, y = make_classification(\n    n_samples=160, n_features=8, random_state=4\n)\npipe = Pipeline([\n    (\"impute\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"median\")),\n    (\"scale\", StandardScaler()),\n    (\"select\", SelectKBest(score_func=f_classif, k=5)),\n    (\"model\", LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000))\n])\nscores = cross_val_score(pipe, X, y, cv=5)\nprint(round(scores.mean(), 3))</code></pre><p>Each cross-validation run refits the imputer, scaler, selector, and classifier on its training fold.</p></section></section>"
    },
    {
      "stem": "Why can random train-test splitting cause Data Leakage in time-series datasets or datasets containing repeated observations from the same users, patients, or devices?",
      "tag": "Advanced · Temporal and group splits",
      "answer": "d",
      "options": [
        "Random splitting is reliable for time series when class proportions stay similar across sets, because balanced labels prevent future information from leaking into earlier records.",
        "Random splitting is appropriate for repeated measurements if each record has a different timestamp, even when the same person or device appears in both evaluation and training.",
        "Time-based splitting solves leakage for every grouped dataset, so observations from the same user may safely appear on both sides if their timestamps are ordered correctly.",
        "Random splitting can expose future information or place related observations in both training and testing sets. Time-based and group-aware splitting help prevent leakage by keeping future or related data separated."
      ],
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> Random splitting assumes observations can be mixed freely, but time and identity can make that unsafe. In a time series, training on later records to predict earlier ones leaks future information. With repeated observations, the same person or device may appear in both sets, letting the model recognize familiar patterns. Imagine a factory machine generating sensor readings each hour. A random split mixes readings from before and after a failure, and may place nearly identical readings on both sides. Use chronological splits or group-aware splits that keep related readings together.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"g2-figure\"><span class=\"g2-kicker\">VISUAL 06 · DATA LEAKAGE</span><h3>Time and identity change the split</h3><div class=\"g2-canvas\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 940 370\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Time-series points t1 through t6 show older training points and newer test points, with grouped patients kept separately\"><rect x=\"1\" y=\"1\" width=\"938\" height=\"368\" rx=\"17\" fill=\"#fcfeff\" stroke=\"#d6e7eb\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"42\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#1f4054\" font-size=\"21\" font-weight=\"900\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">TIME SERIES: PAST → FUTURE</text><path d=\"M78 146H860\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#c0d6de\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"122\" cy=\"146\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#138477\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"122\" y=\"193\" fill=\"#567080\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"800\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">t1</text><circle cx=\"258\" cy=\"146\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#138477\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"258\" y=\"193\" fill=\"#567080\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"800\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">t2</text><circle cx=\"394\" cy=\"146\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#138477\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"394\" y=\"193\" fill=\"#567080\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"800\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">t3</text><circle cx=\"530\" cy=\"146\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#138477\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"530\" y=\"193\" fill=\"#567080\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"800\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">t4</text><circle cx=\"666\" cy=\"146\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#cc6963\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"666\" y=\"193\" fill=\"#567080\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"800\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">t5</text><circle cx=\"802\" cy=\"146\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#cc6963\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"802\" y=\"193\" fill=\"#567080\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"800\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">t6</text><path d=\"M601 93V201\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#cc6963\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"7 7\"/><rect x=\"69\" y=\"75\" width=\"445\" height=\"34\" rx=\"17\" fill=\"#e4f5ed\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"291.5\" y=\"98\" fill=\"#138477\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"800\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Train on earlier timestamps</text><rect x=\"640\" y=\"75\" width=\"241\" height=\"34\" rx=\"17\" fill=\"#ffebe9\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"760.5\" y=\"98\" fill=\"#cc6963\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"800\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Test the future</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"253\" fill=\"#1f4054\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"900\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">GROUPED OBSERVATIONS: KEEP IDENTITIES TOGETHER</text><rect x=\"67\" y=\"280\" width=\"125\" height=\"53\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#eaf5fc\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"129\" y=\"312\" fill=\"#4c83bb\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"770\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">A / day 1</text><rect x=\"211\" y=\"280\" width=\"125\" height=\"53\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#eaf5fc\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"273\" y=\"312\" fill=\"#4c83bb\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"770\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">A / day 2</text><rect x=\"355\" y=\"280\" width=\"125\" height=\"53\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#eaf5fc\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"417\" y=\"312\" fill=\"#4c83bb\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"770\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">B / day 1</text><rect x=\"499\" y=\"280\" width=\"125\" height=\"53\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff2db\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"561\" y=\"312\" fill=\"#936923\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"770\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">C / day 1</text><rect x=\"643\" y=\"280\" width=\"125\" height=\"53\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff2db\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"705\" y=\"312\" fill=\"#936923\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"770\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">C / day 2</text><rect x=\"787\" y=\"280\" width=\"125\" height=\"53\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff2db\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"849\" y=\"312\" fill=\"#936923\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"770\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">D / day 1</text><path d=\"M496 268V347\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#cc6963\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"7 7\"/></svg></div><p class=\"g2-note\">For forecasting or repeated observations, use temporal and group-aware splits rather than arbitrary random rows.</p></section>"
    },
    {
      "stem": "How can Data Leakage be detected and prevented in production Machine Learning systems using point-in-time validation, feature availability checks, and data lineage?",
      "tag": "Advanced · Production availability",
      "answer": "a",
      "options": [
        "Point-in-time validation verifies that features use only information available at prediction time. Feature availability checks and data lineage help detect future information, hidden target details, and contamination between datasets.",
        "Point-in-time validation checks feature timestamps against the model training date rather than each prediction date; this makes future information safe when it came from trusted sources.",
        "Production leakage checks can rely on data lineage alone because knowing the source of a feature proves it was available at prediction time and independent of the target.",
        "Feature availability can be confirmed using the date a dataset was downloaded, while point-in-time tests may combine later events if the historical labels are hidden."
      ],
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> Production leakage checks ask one basic question: was every feature truly available when the prediction would have been made? Point-in-time validation recreates the data as it existed at that moment. Feature availability checks catch fields created too late, while data lineage tracks where each field came from and how it changed. Imagine detecting fraudulent purchases at checkout. A chargeback decision recorded two weeks later must not appear in checkout-time features. Trace the timestamps and data sources, and test with realistic historical snapshots.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"g2-figure\"><span class=\"g2-kicker\">VISUAL 07 · DATA LEAKAGE</span><h3>Point-in-time feature audit</h3><div class=\"g2-canvas\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 940 370\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"At a 09:00 prediction, account balance from 08:15 is available, while the outcome recorded at 11:10 must be blocked\"><rect x=\"1\" y=\"1\" width=\"938\" height=\"368\" rx=\"17\" fill=\"#fcfeff\" stroke=\"#d6e7eb\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"42\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#1f4054\" font-size=\"22\" font-weight=\"900\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">THE PREDICTION HAPPENS AT 09:00</text><path d=\"M468 69V296\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#cc6963\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 8\"/><rect x=\"43\" y=\"89\" width=\"372\" height=\"189\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"#e4f5ed\" stroke=\"#b5dbce\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"68\" y=\"137\" fill=\"#138477\" font-size=\"23\" font-weight=\"900\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">08:15 · Balance</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"177\" fill=\"#567080\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"650\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Source: account ledger</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"226\" fill=\"#138477\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"900\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">✓ Available by 09:00</text><rect x=\"520\" y=\"89\" width=\"372\" height=\"189\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"#ffebe9\" stroke=\"#e9bcb8\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"546\" y=\"137\" fill=\"#cc6963\" font-size=\"23\" font-weight=\"900\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">11:10 · Outcome</text><text x=\"546\" y=\"177\" fill=\"#567080\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"650\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Source: later settlement</text><text x=\"546\" y=\"226\" fill=\"#cc6963\" font-size=\"21\" font-weight=\"900\" tex